From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrvui, wineps, winspool: printers' preferences and properties, with the makers' UI plug-ins

Our Unidrv configuration DLL showed no sheet at all (DocumentProperties
with a prompt returned at once), our PostScript one a single page of its
own, and PrinterProperties was a stub. Now, as Windows' Unidrv and
PostScript cores do (winddiui.h, prcomoem.h, printoem.h references):

- The document's sheet is the printer's features as CPSUI options: Layout
  and Paper/Quality with the standard settings, the Advanced tree with
  every feature of the GPD or PPD (names from the GPD and PPD, standard
  names for the standard options, a PPD's strings in its language's code
  page); OK writes the devmode and answers IDOK (DocumentProperties gave
  CPSUI's own result, not IDOK/IDCANCEL).
- PrinterProperties calls the driver's DrvDevicePropertySheets: Device
  Settings with the printer's own features (GPD *FeatureType:
  PRINTER_PROPERTY, PPD InstallableOptions), kept with the printer and
  used when printing. AdvancedDocumentProperties works.
- The maker's UI plug-ins (the .ini's OEMConfigFile1...): IPrintOemUI and
  IPrintOemUI2 are loaded, given the core (IPrintOemDriverUI,
  IPrintCoreUI2: settings, features, options, SetOptions) and their part of
  the devmode (OEMDM_*); CommonUIProp adds their options among ours (they
  see ours first), DocumentPropertySheets and DevicePropertySheets add
  their own pages, HideStandardUI hides ours. A UI plug-in without a
  render plug-in keeps the maker's part of the devmode.

Ricoh's PostScript driver now shows its Job/Log page (user ID, locked
print, user code); Lexmark's Universal v2 its options.

Test: test/drvui-gate.sh with test/drvui-plugin.c and test/drvui-probe.c,
our own (mutants SG_MUTANT_UNIDOCUI, UIDEVMODE, UIPLUGIN, UIAPPLY,
PSDOCUI, PRINTERFEATURES, DOCRESULT).
